WEBVTT

00:22.700 --> 00:24.624
Yay! Yay!

00:47.990 --> 00:51.856
October 86 and the mountain air is cold

00:54.520 --> 01:01.115
A student contest flyer printed out in bold They

01:01.195 --> 01:04.316
asked for a brand new anthem to shake the autumn

01:04.396 --> 01:07.597
night. A song to lead the forges out into the

01:07.617 --> 01:10.777
stadium light. We rolled a tape machine into our

01:10.817 --> 01:14.078
basement room. And rode a thunderclap to make

01:14.158 --> 01:18.199
the valley boom. 60,000 standing in the maroon

01:18.299 --> 01:21.180
and orange sea. Waiting for the signal, let's

01:21.260 --> 01:24.521
CPI with me. Feel the concrete tremble

01:24.701 --> 01:28.081
underneath your feet. Hear the loudest house in

01:28.121 --> 01:29.522
college sports repeat.

01:32.443 --> 01:35.364
Under the Saturday night lights Inside the

01:35.424 --> 01:38.745
crucible Where the sound of the engine makes us

01:38.865 --> 01:41.786
invincible Hear the forger's call Echoing

01:41.806 --> 01:45.387
across the sky Raise the maroon and orange

01:45.447 --> 01:48.848
banners high When the tunnel opens up and the

01:48.868 --> 01:54.210
speakers roar We're not just a basement band

01:54.670 --> 01:55.210
anymore

02:02.208 --> 02:05.351
Tyler on the drums like a marching thunder line.

02:05.852 --> 02:09.735
Evan on the bass keeping clockwork time. Analog

02:09.775 --> 02:12.878
synths rising like a rocket on the pad. Pouring

02:13.018 --> 02:16.262
out every ounce of fire that we had. From the

02:16.322 --> 02:20.305
press box roof down to the 50 yard line. 60,000

02:20.366 --> 02:23.789
voices singing every single line. 60,000

02:24.049 --> 02:27.331
standing in the maroon and orange sea Waiting

02:27.391 --> 02:30.373
for the signal, it's CPI with me Feel the

02:30.433 --> 02:34.015
concrete tremble underneath your feet Hear the

02:34.215 --> 02:36.957
